==Fighting==
[[File:Hydra poison splats.png|thumb|left|250px|The poison splats launched by the Hydra.]]
Hydras start off with a random combat style at the start of the battle, switching after three attacks, regardless if they hit or not. The magic attack appears as a trio of three dark green trails of spit shot from the left head, and arching to the player (not to be confused with the poison splats, which are light green orbs), while the ranged attack looks like a poisonous barb or thorn being launched at the player from the right head, moving straight forward.

The middle head of the hydra can also spit poison at three random tiles (one at the player's location, two elsewhere), dealing 4 poison damage every two ticks (or 1 to 2 damage if the player has [[poison]] immunity) when the player is standing on one. The initial splat has a 3x3 AoE. This attack is used on every twelfth attack and does not count towards the three attacks Hydras use before switching attack styles. If counting the Hydra's attacks to anticipate the poison splats, players should note that leaving combat does not reset a Hydra's attack sequence, and beware of Hydras that have attacked other players who have left or only passed through the area.

Hydras can drop their [[Hydra's eye|eyes]], [[Hydra's fang|fangs]], and [[Hydra's heart|hearts]], which are used to create the [[brimstone ring]]. Much like [[dark totem]] pieces, the body parts are dropped in order and additional body parts can only be obtained once players have one of each part.

In addition, they can also drop their [[Hydra tail|tail]], which is combined with a [[dragonbone necklace]] and a [[bonecrusher]] to create the [[bonecrusher necklace]].
